2 CONC s question is as difficult as for Mr. Anders. We're not sure who his father was; he could be a descendant by Jon Tordsson Benkestok in 1435, but the chronological reasons, not the son, perhaps son. He could also be the son of Tord
2 CONC  Trondsson, mentioned 1473. What speaks against this is that Torleiv, who had embede 1502, must have been of legal age in 1497, something Tord any sons can not have been. I [Tore H. Vigerust] will later argue that Torleiv must hav
