2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/ad/29/33/29/5344483964d2a379/alstadhaug_kirke_skogn_nord-trondelag_original.jpg?hash=4f0bd1554d29ea5b4a8cad1023ddac03afe7c7bacc65a9085f43ef57e695b595.1797667199
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Alstadhaug Kirke, Skogn, Nord-Trøndelag
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE He matriculated at the University of Rostock in 1561, became Canon in Trondheim and Parish Priest in Beitstad for ten years, 1565 to 1575. Then he was Parish Priest in Frosta for three years. Finally he became Parish Priest at Sko
2 CONC gn, where he succeeded his brother Mikkel in 1578. He lived at Flovik farm in Skogn. During this time he had support from a prebend, but he had to give it up in September 1578, when he, under a royal letter of 8 August of that yea
2 CONC r, took over St. Olav's prebend, which his deceased brother had.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rafael Lund writes about him in 1585, describing the big bell which hangs in Alstahaug Church.  It is incribed, "Mortem præsento. Plebem voco. Congrego clerum campana. Memor esto tui morituri viator. D: Christophorus Sigvardi 1581
2 CONC ." The translation is "I proclaim death. I call the people. I bell, call the Parish together. Wanderer, remember that you shall die. Herr Christopher Sigvardi. 1581." It is clear that Herr Christopher had purchased the bell in 158
2 CONC 1. The smallest of the bells is much older than this one and has a cryptic inscription consisting of signs, and may be as old as the stone church. It is likely that Herr Christopher had made other gifts to the church. By 1580 the 
2 CONC Reformation had proceeded to the point where the huge church festivals in Trondheim Cathedral were at an end. Now this church was to be like any Parish Church. Then they began to sell the expensive priestly clothes that were found
2 CONC  there. Account records were kept and among the entries were "Anno 1580 a chasuble was sold to Herr Christopher in Skogn. It was made of green silk with a red cross, but was a little worn. In addition, a chasuble of a rough gilded
2 CONC  cloth with a black cross, all for 5 daler." In 1581 Herr Christopher bought and old and worn chasuble of green sild. In addition, he bought a blue one with a black cross. The latter was torn in pieces.
