1 NOTE Han var fødd i Bjørgvin 20.oktbr. 1599. Han gjekk skulevegen og vilde verta prest. Fyrst gjekk han paa skule
2 CONT i Bjørgvin, las so ei tid ved universitetet i København og vart student i 1619. So bar det til eit par universitet i
2 CONT utlandet, fyrst til Edinburgh og so , i 1621, til Rostock. Aaret etter kom han heimatt til Bjørgvin. Der var han so
2 CONT ei tid høyrar ved latinskulen. Henrik høyrde til ei baade rik og yrd ætt, og det gjekk snart det gjeteord um han,
2 CONT at han var ein uvanleg lærd mann. Den 31. aug. 1623 vart han kalla til sokneprest paa Voss. Han var daa
2 CONT berre 24 aar gamall. Han gifte seg med den unge enkja etter fyrremannen i embættet, Anders Buch. Det
2 CONT kann godt hena at dette hadde sitt aa segja ved utnemningi. Ho heitte Kristense og var dotter til futen i
2 CONT Hardanger, Mads Jørgensson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik Miltzow var til vissa ein lærd og dugande prest og ein høgvyrd mann. Han var strengt rett-truande og
2 CONT tok det nøgje med emættsførsla. I 1642 vart han prost i Hardanger prosti. I 1645 vart han vald til sendemann
2 CONT for prestane i Bjørgvins bispedøme til stendermøtet som stathaldar Hanibal Sehested hadde kalla saman paa
2 CONT Akershus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik Miltzow var ogso utanfor si embættsførsla ein framtøk og trurøkjen mann, som gjorde mykje godt i
2 CONT kyrkjelyden. Daa kyrkja var til nedfalls, kosta han vøla paa henne av eigne midlar. Men aller mest namngjeten
2 CONT hev han vorte av at han skipa 'Vangens Enkefattighus' eller Voss Enkjeheim, som namnet no er. Og so
2 CONT kosta han upp 'Kjeringastaavo' (seinare umbygd og paabygd til Voss Misjonshotel) og la midlar attaat til
2 CONT vedlikehald og drift.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daa kona døydde, gifta Henrik seg med Kristina, enkja etter futen paa Voss, Lauritz Andersson. Lauritz var
2 CONT av den kjende Heibergætti i Sogn og hadde butt paa Lydvo den tid han var fut. Kristina var dotter til Jakob
2 CONT Jørgenson, lagmann i Gulating.
1 NOTE Picture on page 25 of the Anders Rustad Book
2 CONT
2 CONT      (from the Anders Rustad Ættebok of 1948, translated by Richard Flisrand) After Henrik Miltzow had gone through school in Bergen, he also studied in Copenhagen, Edinburgh, and Rostok, and in 1622 he became a lecturer at the La
2 CONC tin school in Bergen.  The 31st of August, 1623 he became the parish priest at Voss. He was only 24 years old, and remained in Voss until his death.  In 1642 he became head pastor for Handanger.  In 1645, he was selected the repre
2 CONC sentative for the Bergen area, to a conference at Akershus called by Hannibal Sehested. In 1649, Henrik Miltzow bought the Lydvo farm of his former wife, Kirsten.     He founded the "Vangens Poorhouse for Widows", or Voss Widow's 
2 CONC Home", as it is now known.  He also built a "Kjerringastova", the Women's building, which later was enlarged and became, the Voss Misjonshotell.  This burned in the bombing of Voss in April of 1940. The Voss Church was repaired in
2 CONC  his time, paid partly by him.  The old picture Bible in the sacristy of the Voss Church, printed in 1589, was (commissioned? "kostet han innbinding") in 1664.     According to the memorial plaque in the Voss Church, he and his wi
2 CONC fe Kristine were buried under the choir floor in the church.
1 NOTE Picture on page 25 of the Anders Rustad Book
2 CONT
2 CONT      (from the Anders Rustad Ættebok of 1948, translated by Richard Flisrand) After Henrik Miltzow had gone through school in Bergen, he also studied in Copenhagen, Edinburgh, and Rostok, and in 1622 he became a lecturer at the La
2 CONC tin school in Bergen.  The 31st of August, 1623 he became the parish priest at Voss. He was only 24 years old, and remained in Voss until his death.  In 1642 he became head pastor for Handanger.  In 1645, he was selected the repre
2 CONC sentative for the Bergen area, to a conference at Akershus called by Hannibal Sehested. In 1649, Henrik Miltzow bought the Lydvo farm of his former wife, Kirsten.     He founded the "Vangens Poorhouse for Widows", or Voss Widow's 
2 CONC Home", as it is now known.  He also built a "Kjerringastova", the Women's building, which later was enlarged and became, the Voss Misjonshotell.  This burned in the bombing of Voss in April of 1940. The Voss Church was repaired in
2 CONC  his time, paid partly by him.  The old picture Bible in the sacristy of the Voss Church, printed in 1589, was (commissioned? "kostet han innbinding") in 1664.     According to the memorial plaque in the Voss Church, he and his wi
2 CONC fe Kristine were buried under the choir floor in the church.
