1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Rasmus Sørensen Frendesonius (c. 1525 – c. 1599)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasmus Sørensen was the Parish Priest (''Sogneprest'') of Våle in Vestfold. He was a central figure in the clerical and social elite of his time, significantly increasing his family's wealth through strategic land acquisitions and
2 CONC  legal victories.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Career and Social Standing'''
2 CONT * '''Ministry''': Served as the parish priest in Våle, mentioned in records between 1564 and 1589.
2 CONT * '''Legal Victories''': On January 28, 1572, Rasmus and his brother-in-law, Hr. Povel Nielsen (priest in Sande), won a major lawsuit against Hr. Bård Rolvsen regarding the inheritance of '''Kirke-Hole, Hanastad, and Sørum'''. The
2 CONC se lands were part of the vast estate of the lawspeaker Dyre Sevaldsson. The success of this lawsuit was legally rooted in Rasmus’s marriage to the Dyre-lineage heir, Eli Bentsdotter.
2 CONT * '''Commerce''': On January 8, 1586, Hr. Rasmus and his wife Eli purchased fishing rights (salmon) in Mulevik and Frebergsvik (Borre) from Amund Thomasson and Marte Tolvsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and Family'''
2 CONT He married '''Eli Bentsdotter Hård''', the daughter of the Lagmann of Oppland, Bent Andersen Hård, and Kari Dyresdatter. This marriage connected him to the ancient Dyre Sevaldsson (Lunner) lineage and is well-documented through la
2 CONC nd records and judicial acts.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, there is an alternative or additional genealogical theory regarding a second wife. According to historian S.H. Finne-Grønn (1917), Rasmus was also married to a woman named Helga. In the Latin records of Bishop Jens Nilssø
2 CONC n, she is referred to as "cognata" (relative) to the Bishop, which most likely implies she was the sister of the Bishop's wife. This connection would explain the adoption of the "Frendesonius" name by Rasmus’s descendants. Modern 
2 CONC researchers (such as Christiansen and Vigerust) suggest that Helga might have been a first wife, or that Finne-Grønn’s interpretation of the kinship lacks sufficient primary evidence compared to the well-proven marriage with Eli B
2 CONC entsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Known Children''':
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Beritte-Nordre-Sørby/6000000017651592713 '''Beritte'''] '''(Birgitte)''': Married lensmann Vemund Tordssøn Sørby.
2 CONT # '''Søren Rasmussen''': (According to Finne-Grønn) Priest in Lom (d. 1645). Note: While historian Finne-Grønn lists Søren and his son Sakarias (priest in Fåberg) as descendants and attributes their lineage to the "Frendesonius" (
2 CONC Helga) side, some modern researchers point out a lack of primary sources for this specific connection.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The question of Søren Rasmussen’s maternity remains a subject of debate in Norwegian genealogy. While his use of the "Frendesonius" name strongly suggests he was the son of Helga (the Bishop’s relative), the legal inheritance of
2 CONC  lands through the Dyre-lineage by Rasmus’s descendants points towards Eli Bentsdotter as the mother. Modern researchers continue to debate whether Søren was a son from an earlier marriage to Helga or if the "Frendesonius" name wa
2 CONC s adopted through a more distant kinship.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''':
2 CONT * '''Unneberg, Sigurd H.''': "Våle bygdebok 1.1", [https://www.nb.no/items/588161dd24e8ec531783963d9b69e56e?page=87&searchText=Rasmus%20S%C3%B8rensson pp. 64, 74].
2 CONT * '''Christiansen, P. R. B.''': "Dyre Sevaldssons Ætt", NST 35 (1996). (''Focuses on the Dyre-family inheritance and Eli Bentsdotter’s role'').
2 CONT * '''Vigerust, Tore H.''': "Dyre Sevaldssons ætt", Slekt og data 1995, No. 3. [https://admin.slektogdata.no/sites/default/files/2019-08/1995-3.pdf pp. 18-19]. (''Critical analysis of older genealogical theories'').
2 CONT * '''Finne-Grønn, S.H''': "Søfren Rasmussen Frendesonius", NST (1917), [https://www.nb.no/items/1a2d025a8829e3cb914cc26f7593e305?page=1&searchText=Frendesonius pp. 289-291]. (''Original source for the Helga/Frendesonius theory'').
2 CONT
2 CONT Dersom vi ser nærmere på Finne-Grønns artikkel, står det at Hr. Rasmus Sørensen var gift med en Helga som var 'cognata' til biskop Jens Nilsen Frendesonius, dvs mest sannsynlig at Helga var søster til biskopens kone. 
